# Hannaz Tailwind (Play CDN) — iSH friendly

This is a single-file Tailwind starter that uses the Tailwind Play CDN. It is designed to work on iSH (Alpine) on iPhone where Node may not be available.

Files:
- Hannaz1_STEPS.txt       — steps & notes
- Hannaz2_index.html      — Tailwind Play CDN demo (edit this)
- Hannaz3_https_server.py — optional HTTPS server (requires certs)
- Hannaz4_README.md       — this file
- Hannaz5_LICENSE         — MIT license
- Hannaz6_init_git.sh     — helper to init git
- Hannaz7_gitignore       — recommended ignores

Quick start (in iSH):
1. mkdir hannaz-tailwind && cd hannaz-tailwind
2. Copy Hannaz2_index.html into the folder (paste via your editor)
3. Edit the file with your preferred editor in iSH.
4. Preview options:
   - Best: push to GitHub and enable GitHub Pages for browser preview.
   - Local: python3 -m http.server 8000  (may not be reachable from Safari)
   - HTTPS (optional): generate certs with openssl and run Hannaz3_https_server.py

Generating certs (optional):
apk add openssl
mkdir certs
cd certs
openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -nodes -keyout key.pem -out cert.pem -days 365 -subj "/CN=localhost"
cd ..

Run HTTPS server:
chmod +x Hannaz3_https_server.py
python3 Hannaz3_https_server.py --port 8443 --cert certs/cert.pem --key certs/key.pem

Git:
apk add git
git config --global user.name "dadjgh-sudo"
git config --global user.email "Example@icloud.com"
chmod +x Hannaz6_init_git.sh
./Hannaz6_init_git.sh

Notes about iSH and preview:
- iSH may not allow external access to servers it runs; Safari on iOS might not reach them.
- For reliable preview in Safari, push to GitHub and use GitHub Pages (free).